# RANGE ELIMINATION MUST KEY X_{r,D} BY THE WHOLE FILLER, fresh ids included.
# Both existential fillers are complex, so each is named by a FRESH node. A key
# that renders every fresh node alike gives both the same X_{r,_:fresh}; X then
# inherits P and U, which are disjoint, so X is unsatisfiable and so are C1 and C2.
# That is over-derivation — unsoundness — and it made OBI report itself inconsistent.
# Expect: COHERENT, unsatisfiable EMPTY. Removing the range must not change the verdict.
@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

:r a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range :R .

:C1 a owl:Class .
:C2 a owl:Class .
:P  a owl:Class .
:Q  a owl:Class .
:U  a owl:Class .
:V  a owl:Class .
:R  a owl:Class .

:P owl:disjointWith :U .

:C1 rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :r ;
    owl:someValuesFrom [ a owl:Class ; owl:intersectionOf ( :P :Q ) ] ] .

:C2 rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty :r ;
    owl:someValuesFrom [ a owl:Class ; owl:intersectionOf ( :U :V ) ] ] .
